akikoplus.library/--background--               akikoplus.library/--background--

   PURPOSE
	Helpers for programs that move and convert pixels and data: byte
	swaps, chunky to planar, rectangle fills and copies, scaling, YUV
	to ARGB, colour reduction and zlib streams. On a machine with
	AmiCradle's AkikoPlus media board (AmiCradle Team $DA15, product 18,
	ACSV CLASS 5) the board's host does the work with its CPU's vector
	units (AVX2 or SSSE3 on x86, NEON on ARM64); elsewhere the library
	does it on the 68k. Both give the same bytes, so a program needs to
	know none of it. The zlib streams are the exception: the 68k writes
	its own valid zlib streams, not the host zlib's bytes, and each
	side reads the other's.

   HOW IT REACHES THE BOARD
	Through mitchy.library (1), which goes through gfopenservice.device,
	the owner of every ACSV board's rings. The services akiko.swap/1,
	akiko.c2p/1, akiko.fill/1, akiko.scale/1, akiko.convert/1 and
	akiko.z/1 are opened board only (MOF_BOARDONLY) the first time a
	call needs them. If mitchy.library or the board is missing, or the
	board cannot be reached during a call, the 68k version runs.

   SMALL JOBS
	A request to the board costs a round trip through the device, so a
	job smaller than AP_SetThreshold's bytes (4096 to start) stays on
	the 68k. AP_SetMode chooses the 68k or the board for every job.

   BUILDS
	The basebuild has the 68k versions. A build with AP_NO_FALLBACK,
	for machines that always have the board, leaves them out (about a
	third of the size): AP_Status then lacks APSF_FALLBACK, and the
	calls answer AP_ERR_NOBOARD on a machine without the board.

   MEMORY
	Any memory, Chip or Fast; the device keeps the data cache right.
	Every structure gives each buffer's length, and the library refuses
	a job that would pass it (AP_ERR_BADARGS).

   VERSIONS
	1 (8.11.2026) to the board through gfopenservice.device; no 68k zlib.
	2 (9.11.2026) through mitchy.library; the 68k zlib streams;
	AP_SetMode and AP_Query. The calls of 1 keep their offsets,
	arguments and structures.

akikoplus.library/AP_Status                         akikoplus.library/AP_Status

   NAME
	AP_Status -- what the library has (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	flags = AP_Status()
	D0

	ULONG AP_Status(void);

   FUNCTION
	Opens the board's services, the first time, and says what is there.

   RESULT
	flags - APSF_BOARD: the board's services are open. APSF_FALLBACK
	        (V2): the 68k versions are built in.

akikoplus.library/AP_SwapCopy                     akikoplus.library/AP_SwapCopy

   NAME
	AP_SwapCopy -- byte-swap units into another buffer (V1)
	AP_SwapInPlace -- byte-swap units where they are (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_SwapCopy(dst, src, count, unit)
	D0                  A0   A1   D0     D1

	LONG AP_SwapCopy(APTR, CONST_APTR, ULONG, ULONG);

	error = AP_SwapInPlace(data, count, unit)
	D0                     A0    D0     D1

	LONG AP_SwapInPlace(APTR, ULONG, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Reverses the bytes of count units of unit bytes (2, 4 or 8): little-
	endian data from a PC file to the 68k's order, or back. dst may be
	src.

   RESULT
	0, or AP_ERR_BADARGS for another unit. A count of 0 does nothing.

akikoplus.library/AP_SwapInterleaved       akikoplus.library/AP_SwapInterleaved

   NAME
	AP_SwapInterleaved -- byte-swap the fields of records (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_SwapInterleaved(data, layout, count, stride)
	D0                         A0    A1      D0     D1

	LONG AP_SwapInterleaved(APTR, CONST_STRPTR, ULONG, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	count records, stride bytes apart, each starting with the fields
	layout names, one digit a field, its size in bytes: "444221" is
	three longs, two words and a byte. Each field's bytes are reversed;
	bytes after the last field are left alone.

   RESULT
	0, or AP_ERR_BADARGS (a digit not 1, 2, 4 or 8, or fields longer
	than stride).

akikoplus.library/AP_C2P                               akikoplus.library/AP_C2P

   NAME
	AP_C2P -- chunky pixels to bitplanes (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_C2P(args)
	D0             A0

	LONG AP_C2P(CONST struct APC2P *);

   FUNCTION
	ap_Width x ap_Height 8-bit pixels, ap_ChunkyPitch bytes a row, into
	ap_Depth (1-8) planes: plane p of row y starts at ap_Planes +
	y * ap_RowStride + p * ap_PlaneStride, so planes apart and
	interleaved bitmaps both work. Bit p of each pixel goes to plane p;
	bits past the width in a row's last byte are 0. Into Chip RAM
	directly, for a display.

   RESULT
	0, or AP_ERR_BADARGS.

akikoplus.library/AP_Fill                             akikoplus.library/AP_Fill

   NAME
	AP_Fill -- fill a rectangle (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_Fill(args)
	D0              A0

	LONG AP_Fill(CONST struct APFill *);

   FUNCTION
	Fills ap_Width x ap_Height pixels of ap_BytesPerPixel (1-4) bytes at
	ap_Dest, ap_Pitch bytes a row, with ap_Pixel (big-endian, in its low
	bytes).

   RESULT
	0, or AP_ERR_BADARGS.

akikoplus.library/AP_CopyRect                     akikoplus.library/AP_CopyRect

   NAME
	AP_CopyRect -- copy a rectangle (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_CopyRect(args)
	D0                  A0

	LONG AP_CopyRect(CONST struct APCopy *);

   FUNCTION
	Copies ap_Width x ap_Height pixels of ap_BytesPerPixel bytes from
	ap_Src (ap_SrcPitch bytes a row) to ap_Dest (ap_DestPitch). The two
	must not overlap.

   RESULT
	0, or AP_ERR_BADARGS.

akikoplus.library/AP_Scale                           akikoplus.library/AP_Scale

   NAME
	AP_Scale -- scale an image (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_Scale(args)
	D0               A0

	LONG AP_Scale(CONST struct APScale *);

   FUNCTION
	Scales ap_SrcWidth x ap_SrcHeight to ap_DestWidth x ap_DestHeight,
	sampling at pixel centres. ap_Filter APSCALE_NEAREST (1-4 bytes a
	pixel) or APSCALE_BILINEAR (3 or 4 bytes a pixel; 8 bits of weight
	each way, rounded).

   RESULT
	0, AP_ERR_BADARGS, or AP_ERR_NOMEM (the 68k's column table).

akikoplus.library/AP_YUVToARGB                   akikoplus.library/AP_YUVToARGB

   NAME
	AP_YUVToARGB -- 4:2:0 YUV to ARGB32 (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	error = AP_YUVToARGB(args)
	D0                   A0

	LONG AP_YUVToARGB(CONST struct APYUV *);

   FUNCTION
	BT.601, studio range: ap_Y full size, ap_U and ap_V half each way
	(ap_UVPitch bytes a row), into A, R, G, B bytes (A 255), the
	integer formula the board's akiko.convert/1 gives.

   RESULT
	0, or AP_ERR_BADARGS.

akikoplus.library/AP_Quantise                     akikoplus.library/AP_Quantise

   NAME
	AP_Quantise -- ARGB32 to 8-bit by median cut (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	colours = AP_Quantise(args)
	D0                    A0

	LONG AP_Quantise(CONST struct APQuant *);

   FUNCTION
	Reduces ap_Width x ap_Height ARGB32 pixels to at most ap_Colours
	(2-256) by median cut over a 15-bit histogram, writing a byte a
	pixel to ap_Dest and 4 bytes a colour (0, R, G, B) to ap_Palette.

   RESULT
	The colours used, or AP_ERR_BADARGS or AP_ERR_NOMEM (the 68k needs
	224 KB to work in).

akikoplus.library/AP_Compress                     akikoplus.library/AP_Compress

   NAME
	AP_Compress -- a zlib stream (V1)
	AP_Decompress -- data from a zlib stream (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	bytes = AP_Compress(src, dst, srcLength, dstLength, level)
	D0                  A0   A1   D0         D1         D2

	LONG AP_Compress(CONST_APTR, APTR, ULONG, ULONG, ULONG);

	bytes = AP_Decompress(src, dst, srcLength, dstLength)
	D0                    A0   A1   D0         D1

	LONG AP_Decompress(CONST_APTR, APTR, ULONG, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	The zlib format (RFC 1950), level 0-9. On the board, the host's
	zlib; on the 68k (V2), the library's own: stored blocks at level 0,
	fixed Huffman codes over a 32 KB window above it. Both sides read
	any zlib stream.

   RESULT
	The bytes written, or AP_ERR_TOOSMALL (dst has no room),
	AP_ERR_BADARGS (bad arguments, or a damaged stream), AP_ERR_NOMEM.
	V1 answered AP_ERR_NOBOARD without the board; V2 does so only in a
	board-only build.

akikoplus.library/AP_SetThreshold             akikoplus.library/AP_SetThreshold

   NAME
	AP_SetThreshold -- the smallest job for the board (V1)

   SYNOPSIS
	old = AP_SetThreshold(bytes)
	D0                    D0

	ULONG AP_SetThreshold(ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	In APMODE_AUTO, a job of fewer bytes than this stays on the 68k
	(4096 to start). The bytes are the data's size: pixels times their
	bytes, or the bytes swapped. For every program using the library.

   RESULT
	The threshold before.

akikoplus.library/AP_SetMode                       akikoplus.library/AP_SetMode

   NAME
	AP_SetMode -- where the work runs (V2)

   SYNOPSIS
	old = AP_SetMode(mode)
	D0               D0

	ULONG AP_SetMode(ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	APMODE_AUTO (the start): the board for a job of the threshold or
	more. APMODE_68K: the 68k always. APMODE_BOARD: the board always,
	when it is fitted. For every program using the library: for tests
	and timings (AkikoTest), not for programs to leave set.

   RESULT
	The mode before. Another value changes nothing.

akikoplus.library/AP_Query                           akikoplus.library/AP_Query

   NAME
	AP_Query -- the library's state (V2)

   SYNOPSIS
	value = AP_Query(what)
	D0               D0

	LONG AP_Query(ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	APQ_SERVICES: APF_* of the board's services that are open.
	APQ_METHOD: the board's METHOD register, the vector units its host
	uses (0 plain C, 1 SSSE3, 2 AVX2, 3 NEON), -1 without the board.
	APQ_MODE, APQ_THRESHOLD: as set.
	APQ_LASTRAN: where the last call ran, from any task: 1 the board,
	0 the 68k, -1 none yet.

   RESULT
	The value, or AP_ERR_BADARGS for another what.
